 "first_pass_caveat": "Phases 01-04 have no subphases, so each is scored as ONE phase-wide unit (first verdict of the whole phase) while phases 05-15 are scored per subphase or work order; the 8 of 38 first-pass rate therefore mixes two granularities (4 of the 38 units are whole phases, all of which were not approved first time; checked by hand for the first verdicts of phases 01, 02, 03 and 04). The hand audit of phase 03 (hand_audit_phase_03) found the parser undercounts verdict events there (11 counted against 14 by hand) because some verdicts are in prose or under 'STATUS: COMPLETE'; the first-pass result of that phase is the same either way. The rate is a heuristic over records, not a count of agent attempts, and no per-agent rate can be derived (see gaps).",
